# .dockerignore -- Week 11. Neither image COPYs data/ (it's mounted as a
# volume at runtime -- see Dockerfile.api's comment on why), so excluding it
# here just keeps the build context small and the build fast: without this,
# every `docker build` would zip up and send the full corpus/model/index
# files to the Docker daemon even though no COPY instruction ever uses them.
data/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.git/
tests/
.github/
*.md
